From: Aurélien Pommel <aurelien.pommel@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gpio: rockchip: use the vendor kernel's fixed GPIO numbers

Stock-built software drives pins through /sys/class/gpio by number
(gpio150 for the headphone amp, gpio20 for rumble), so bank N must start at
N*32 as on the vendor kernel.

---
--- a/drivers/gpio/gpio-rockchip.c
+++ b/drivers/gpio/gpio-rockchip.c
@@ -582,7 +582,8 @@
 	bank->gpio_chip = rockchip_gpiolib_chip;
 
 	gc = &bank->gpio_chip;
-	gc->base = -1;
+	/* The vendor kernel's fixed numbers (gpio150 = GPIO4_C6). */
+	gc->base = bank->bank_num * 32;
 	gc->ngpio = bank->nr_pins;
 	gc->label = bank->name;
 	gc->parent = bank->dev;
